WEBVTT

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.940
H-Hikaru...

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.150
It's been a long time.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.360
You're looking well, Daigo-kun.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.990
<i>He can't pitch anymore...</i>

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:21.840
<i>...because of that injury.</i>

00:01:55.090 --> 00:02:00.470
<b>Cinderella's Magic</b>

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:05.520
<i>So I guess Sakaguchi must be
his mother's maiden name.</i>

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.060
<i>He's gotten taller and
doesn't wear glasses now.</i>

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.310
<i>But it's definitely him.</i>

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.280
Huh? What is it?

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.360
Hey, Mutsu. You said you used
to be friends with that guy?

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.310
His name's Sakaguchi-kun, right?

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:22.470
You need to introduce us afterwards!

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.890
I think we'd make a wonderful couple!

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:25.870
Excuse me?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.420
I won't let you hit.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.560
Play!

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.650
Boss, has Sakaguchi ever 
caught any of Mario's pitches?

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.470
Hm, well, this is actually Mario's A-Team debut.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.010
So it's his first time catching for him.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.180
<i>This is ridiculous.</i>

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:50.190
<i>Sure, as an A-Team regular, 
Hikaru is a better catcher than me,</i>

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:53.250
<i>but there's no way he'll catch 
those Mario-balls on his first try.</i>

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.110
Ball!

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:01.450
Huh? What'd you say?

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:06.140
I don't care if they're "Mario-balls"
or whatever, but don't throw them.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:07.660
Just throw fastballs.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.450
I was throwin' fastballs 'cause Inoue
can't catch anythin' else, and they got hits!

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.220
As the A-Team catcher,
you should catch 'em just fine, right?!

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:18.370
So it's Inoue's fault you went to pieces?

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.280
No, it was your own fault.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.350
Catchers aren't babysitters.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.640
Stop being a baby.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:30.680
Ball!

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.350
Two balls, one strike!

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.000
Nice, Hikaru!

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.240
What are they doing?

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.320
We switched in Sakaguchi,
but nothing's changed!

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.200
<i>What the hell is this?</i>

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.900
<i>How can the A-Team catcher be so crap?</i>

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:46.160
<i>He acts all high 'n' mighty, but he's just
scared my Mario-balls'll be too hot to handle.</i>

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.390
<i>Well, screw you.</i>

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.080
<i>I'm gonna...</i>

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.160
<i>...embarrass you!</i>

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.580
It's a Mario-ball!

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.380
<i>He... He caught it?!</i>

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:02.470
Strike!

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.430
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.640
Timeout.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:07.570
Timeout!

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.100
<i>O-Oh crap!</i>

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.560
<i>He's gonna kill me!</i>

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.770
That was a good breaking ball.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:21.520
Your form wasn't shaky, and with that
trajectory, they won't get any easy hits.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.570
And what's more,

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.830
your bad personality trait of not cowing to
a senior catcher makes you pitcher material.

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:32.760
But your days are numbered if you're 
already relying on that breaking ball.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:38.810
Your number one weapon is your fastball 
with either topspin or backspin, isn't it?

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.520
Count: two balls, two strikes.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:47.330
Play!

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.200
Think about when your control went to pot.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.180
How you wavered when
the count went against you.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.730
How you allowed them to hit.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.540
It was probably your mental
game that let you down.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.930
Infuse your fastball with your spirit!

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:01.730
That breaking ball is nothing 
more than Mario-ball #2.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.490
A fastball thrown with your abilities...

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.280
...is the real Mario-ball #1!

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:09.870
Strike! You're out!

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:11.830
Hell yeah!

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.960
Fuurin

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.960
Fuurin

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.960
Tsujidou

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.960
Tsujidou

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:24.940
Guess we didn't score any runs.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:28.430
I'm sorry. If only I'd tagged up...

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:31.440
Daigo, what's wrong?

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:37.660
I'm going to join my middle school 
baseball team and make a comeback!

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.310
So...

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:45.150
Let's meet up again someday and 
form the strongest battery ever!

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.740
Hello? Daigo!

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:52.680
Oh, uh, right. We're changing sides.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.410
Their cleanup's an acquaintance of yours?

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:00.080
Acquaintance? Yeah, that's about right.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.590
All right, top of the order with our starters.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:04.840
Go overturn this eight-run gap.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.050
Yes, sir!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:16.330
<i>Batting first, shortstop, Kunitomo Luigi-kun.</i>

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.750
<i>I wonder if Daigo's all right.</i>

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.400
<i>He doesn't seem himself.</i>

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:25.830
<i>Did something happen between them?</i>

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.320
Play!

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.060
Nishina!

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.680
Yer pitches're good!

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.570
Ain't nothin' to be scared of!

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:33.660
We're still leadin'!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:34.910
Attack!

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:36.410
Huh?

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.040
Strike!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.010
You're over-rotating, Luigi!

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:40.620
No need to go big!

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:41.920
Annoying ass.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:45.830
I'm gunning to be the 
number one power hitter!

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:48.670
I got it!

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:01.140
Safe!

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.870
Y-You said you had it!

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.730
Oh, whoops, my bad.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.710
And there it is!
Luigi slugs it into the infield!

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:12.700
Nice almost-hit!

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.110
Shut up!

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:18.900
<i>Batting second, center field, Katsuno-kun.</i>

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.260
Play!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.460
<i>He ain't takin' a lead.</i>

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.680
<i>I guess he's not going to steal.</i>

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:32.840
He's running!

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.510
What?!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.350
Safe!

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:40.770
H-Hey!

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.350
Oh, whoopsie.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:46.200
Someone, help!

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.400
This girl's beating me up 
while pretending to tag me out!

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:51.290
One ball, no strikes.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.670
<i>I can't believe he stole with zero lead.</i>

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:55.870
<i>How embarrassing.</i>

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.190
<i>Damn, he tricked us.</i>

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:02.160
<i>I figured he wasn't gonna run, 
so I didn't do a slide step.</i>

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:07.870
Second!

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.010
Whew, close one.

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:13.810
<i>What the hell are you doing, Daigo?</i>

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:16.640
<i>I signaled for a pickoff. Don't just miss it!</i>

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:19.440
<i>Crap. Did I miss that?</i>

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:21.980
<i>If we'd thrown when she signaled,
it would've been close.</i>

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.050
Hey, hey! Hey, hey!

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:30.260
We still got the lead!

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.320
The runner don't matter. Ignore him!

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.210
<i>Something's up with you, Daigo.</i>

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:38.770
<i>You're not giving out detailed instructions,
and you're not shouting to us.</i>

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:41.540
Ball!

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:45.290
He's so green, lettin' his
rhythm get disrupted like that.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.000
<i>Look who's talking.</i>

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.430
Hey, hey!

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:49.480
Shut up!

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:52.920
Ball!

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:53.980
Ball four!

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.890
Yes, runners on first and second!

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:00.460
<i>Batting third, catcher, Sakaguchi-kun.</i>

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:04.940
You getting distracted?

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:09.650
Don't worry so much about me
not being a pitcher anymore.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.530
It's not like it was your fault.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:15.560
And anyway, even if I could still pitch,

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:18.620
I wouldn't want to be in a battery with you.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.950
Not when you're this mediocre.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.800
M-Mediocre?

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:29.960
Well, I'm sure you're doing the best you can.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:35.880
<i>Screw this.</i>

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.680
<i>I'm not gonna let them kick
my ass in front of that old fart!</i>

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.640
Ball!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:45.890
My dad told me you played
baseball over at Fuurin Middle.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:50.780
I felt for you when I heard your team got
suspended for six months over that scandal.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.020
Seriously, you're so unlucky.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:55.570
Will you just shut up?!
We're in the middle of a game!

00:09:55.570 --> 00:10:00.030
But even so, I was really disappointed in you.

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:01.990
He's running!

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:06.960
I thought, "Why's he playing 
house in this environment?"

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:11.250
Safe!

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:13.710
Heck yeah! Double steal!

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:16.680
That's our Luigi! Perfect setup!

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:19.770
Not only did your throw to third
take nearly three seconds,

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:22.180
you also didn't throw to the optimal spot.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:26.700
What on earth have you been doing 
these last two years, Daigo-kun?

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:29.800
While I went through hell
to rehabilitate myself

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.650
and gave everything to 
become a starter for Tsujidou,

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:37.150
you were busy collecting
girlfriends, by the looks of it.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:45.080
It's really disappointing to see 
Shigeno Goro's son slacking off like this.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.200
There it goes!

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.080
A perfect three-run homer!

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:55.800
Now we're only five behind!

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.680
Just kidding!

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:06.140
Enjoy your girl party.

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:14.020
Fuurin

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:14.020
Fuurin

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:14.020
Tsujidou

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:14.020
Tsujidou

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:14.010
<i>I don't know...</i>

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:18.060
<i>...what happened after that.</i>

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:26.470
<i>And before it registered...</i>

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.380
Strike three!

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:38.030
You're out!

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:40.830
<i>...the game was over.</i>

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.260
Fuurin

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.260
Fuurin

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.260
Tsujidou

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.260
Tsujidou

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:49.230
Want to know why I became a catcher?

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:54.060
I decided to follow in my dad's footsteps
and play catcher in the major leagues.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:57.770
So I think you and I are
just in different worlds now.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:10.410
Wh-What?!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:14.190
You're saying Kunitomo 
is now Tsujidou's coach?

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:16.380
Ow...

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:19.890
Hm? Were you so shocked
you made your wound reopen?

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.760
But yeah, I was really surprised.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:27.040
That old jackass is coaching
at the school his two sons go to.

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.410
I got all pissed and took to the mound,

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:32.640
but halfway through, their A-Team 
showed up and pulverized us.

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:35.660
They slaughtered us 20-14.

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:39.320
Wait, 20-14? But that means
 you guys scored 14 runs.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:45.030
No, we were given a 10-run handicap,
so the real score was 20-4.

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:49.880
Instead of getting revenge, 
I just got embarrassed some more.

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:54.620
It's totally his fault that
we're on this all-girls team,

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:58.220
but he still went out of his 
way to grind us into the dirt.

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:00.050
Excuse us.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:01.410
Yo.

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:02.960
Hey, he's alive.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:06.430
Wh-What? You came too?

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:09.950
I mean, we <i>are</i> teammates.
Of course we'd come check on you.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:14.080
Today's practice was canceled,
so we had nothin' better to do.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.430
Tao-senpai and the others 
immediately said "hard pass" to coming.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:20.940
To be honest, I wanted to go shopping, but...

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.400
Did you come here to bully me?

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.360
So when do you think you'll be out?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.800
Oh, probably the day after tomorrow.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.130
But it'll likely be another month 
till I can come to practice again.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:33.460
Huh? That long?

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:34.760
He's lying.

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.830
Earlier, the doctor said he 
shouldn't need more than a week.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:41.760
Y'all better be prepared.

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:47.660
After that humiliatin' loss yesterday,
the captain's gonna be harder'n ever on us.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.790
Today's day off is the calm before the storm.

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:55.140
Well, since it was frustratin' for
us too, I actually welcome it.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.490
You still just want to be our manager?

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.780
Yes, if that's all right.

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:09.280
But why, Chiyo?

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:10.840
Wouldn't you rather play?

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:13.200
You got a base hit, made an amazing play,

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.720
and I think you'd be
a great addition to the team!

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.330
But I only managed those things once.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:21.130
Towards the end, I was
making error after error.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.160
I basically just held everyone back.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.500
Everyone, you say?

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:28.580
Don't you mean you held 
a <i>certain someone</i> back?

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:30.440
Put a sock in it, Sis!

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.830
Don't make me flick your forehead!
I know it's your weakness!

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:35.950
Not the forehead!

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:42.400
Chiba-kun will be back soon,
so I'm fine with a supporting role.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.460
I'll go get things ready for practice now.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:50.280
Huh? How come you're in sweats?

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:51.910
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:51.910
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:51.910
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:51.990
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:51.990
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:51.990
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:52.070
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:52.070
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:52.070
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.450
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.450
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.450
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:58.910
She said she'd rather be the manager than
the one who sucks and holds the team back.

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:00.270
What?

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.410
Daigo's late, isn't he?

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:08.550
What's goin' on? I figured he'd be
workin' us to the bone from first light.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:10.000
Should we just start?

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:11.890
I think we should wait.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:16.350
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:16.350
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:16.350
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:16.350
It's time, so let's get started.
We'll do our regular warm-up.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:18.310
One more time!

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:23.940
What are you doing? You should've had that!

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.780
You're moving too slow 
and tiring too quickly!

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.510
Yikes. Scary.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:31.910
Looks like Daigo isn't
 our only drill sergeant.

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:33.180
All right.

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:34.870
You can get in position, Anita!

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:35.740
What?

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:38.290
Ya musta pitched around
100 balls the other day.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:42.830
Stick to makin' light adjustments today.
We oughta wait for the captain to instruct us.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:46.070
I'm fine, so just crouch down
already! 100 balls is nothing!

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.500
Jeez!

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.380
Well, I get how ya feel, though.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:56.350
<i>I get why he chose them over us.</i>

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.060
<i>But don't go thinking that decision...</i>

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:04.770
<i>...broke me!</i>

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:10.900
<i>See, just making it to regionals was too
small a goal for me to get properly fired up!</i>

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:16.810
Daigo?

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:19.290
Captain?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:20.510
Morning!

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:22.370
You're definitely not early.

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:25.500
Since when does the captain
roll in 30 minutes late?

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:28.510
Sorry, sorry. I overslept.

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:31.450
Th-That's pretty rare for you.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:32.340
Is it?

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:35.070
You've got to be more careful.

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:35.800
Huh?

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:40.440
After that huge loss, all of us shook it off
and showed up to morning practice.

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:43.290
So why aren't you running to
get here when you're late?

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:45.330
You didn't contact anyone, either.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.150
Daigo. Are you listening to me?

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.100
Oh, come on.

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:51.840
What's the big deal, Mutsuko?

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.610
You're so scary.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:54.950
Daigo?

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:58.780
This is a club, right? Let's just have fun.

00:16:59.010 --> 00:16:59.870
Huh?

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:02.730
Have fun?

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.380
We <i>are</i> having fun.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:09.360
But after Tsujidou blew us away,
we were all obviously upset.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:12.780
We know we've got to try harder.
That's why we have morning practice.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:13.860
And you show up late—

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:14.960
Cram it.

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:15.630
Huh?

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:18.260
So what if I'm late?

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:21.760
In fact, I've been pushing 
us too hard up to now.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:26.190
Every day, baseball this, baseball that, team
this, team that. We were like mindless idiots.

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:27.810
Huh?

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:30.770
We're students, which
means we also have to study.

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:34.850
We have to sleep well, eat well,
and relax. Enjoy our youth, basically.

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:36.700
It's not like we're baseball pros.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:39.530
Once I'm warmed up, I'll take over
hitting for fielding practice.

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:41.490
J-Just a minute, Daigo!

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.410
What are you saying all of a sudden?!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.710
Was losing to Tsujidou such a shock,
you've lost all motivation?

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.990
So what, because we didn't stand
a chance, you're doing a 180 now?

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:55.920
I'm not doing a 180. I just think
we don't need to go insane over it.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:18:00.640
Our goal doesn't need to be any higher
than making it to regionals, that's all.

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.060
<b>Music Room</b>

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:14.440
Sakura-senpai, yer thinkin' it too, aren't ya?

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:16.470
S'jus' plain weird.

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:18.850
Ya listenin', Senpai?

00:18:18.850 --> 00:18:19.910
Oh, uh, yeah.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.730
How're we meant to keep our morale up if our
captain's like that? What happened to him?

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:26.590
I mean, Tsujidou <i>was</i> seriously good.

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:29.130
I don't think there's 
anything we can do about it.

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:32.130
He said he wanted to carry on like
before. What's wrong with that?

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:35.850
I was relieved with how calm he was about it.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:39.340
It would've been worse if he'd said
 beating Tsujidou was our new goal.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:43.380
Nishina will probably be mad
'cause their coach betrayed him,

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:46.040
but because of that,
we've got our team of girls,

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.310
so if anything, I'd say, "Thanks, dude."

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:52.270
So yer sayin' yer fine 
with that humiliatin' loss?!

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:53.920
I don't feel humiliated.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:57.440
I mean, we were playing against men.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:04.080
You saw their physique,
their hits, and their speed, right?

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:08.570
Those weren't boys anymore. They were men.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:12.010
Daigo's just being realistic.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:16.720
It'd be cruel to ask more from us, and he
understands we don't have more to give.

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:21.780
The time when we can go toe to toe with
the boys is at an end. The party's over.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:26.700
The clock struck midnight a long time ago.

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:29.350
Cinderella's magic spell...

00:19:31.260 --> 00:19:32.830
...has broken.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:37.880
Bye. I'm leavin' early.

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:39.780
I'll go on ahead, Chiyo.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:40.750
Good job today.

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:41.820
Good job!

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:44.080
Hey, do you know where Daigo is?

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.490
Oh, he was the first to leave.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:48.340
He asked if we could lock up.

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:53.980
Say no to crunching at club.
Say yes to the reformed work style.

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:55.130
Or whatever.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:58.610
If Shigeno-senpai's given up 'cause 
he doesn't want you girls getting hurt,

00:19:58.610 --> 00:20:00.970
the first thing to do is 
tell him what you want, no?

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:04.310
Not that I know anything about Cinderella.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.090
Y-You heard us earlier?

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:09.320
You can hear everything through the window.

00:20:09.820 --> 00:20:15.150
Anyway, if we just carry on like before,
we won't even scratch Tsujidou.

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:18.520
Saying that, I don't know how it is for you girls.

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:21.860
Oh, by the way, I wanted to ask
a favor, since you're the vice-captain.

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:22.360
Yes?

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:26.050
The sun's going down earlier now,
and practice isn't long enough.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:28.440
Please ask if we can use the floodlights.

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:29.580
The lights?

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:33.180
The captain was talking about
studying and youth and stuff like that,

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:34.790
but all I have is baseball.

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:37.920
I wanna stay later and practice,
even if it's just me.

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:39.340
Thanks.

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:47.760
Nishina-kun is really motivated.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:50.110
Yeah. I understand 
where he's coming from.

00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:52.230
I bet Anita would agree to stay later, too.

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:54.440
And what about you?

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.110
Huh?

00:20:56.050 --> 00:20:56.750
Yeah...

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.770
I was also upset about losing,

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:02.530
but I can see Tao's point too.

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:06.730
We've been practicing as much
as we thought we could handle,

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:10.420
but against Tsujidou, we stood no chance.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:15.920
It makes you wonder if, as girls,
we <i>have</i> reached our limit.

00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:19.880
If we intensify our practices, 
someone might get hurt.

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:24.240
We're already short on players, so any
injury would rule us out of tournaments.

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:25.400
And what's more...

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:32.310
I might be the one who was
the most affected emotionally.

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:33.100
Huh?

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:39.290
I couldn't get a single player 
from Tsujidou's A-Team out.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:41.500
They hit back-to-back home runs.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:45.180
As the vice-captain, I put up a front 
and tried to keep morale high.

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:49.250
But if Daigo and Tao say we
should just carry on like before,

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:51.030
who am I to say otherwise?

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:52.650
I can't say anything!

00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:54.250
Not when I'm this weak!

00:21:56.710 --> 00:22:01.340
Dream

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:04.160
I'm home... Huh?

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:06.100
Welcome back, Izumi.

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:09.640
Hey, Mom, did Daigo come home early?

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:12.880
Yeah. He was very slow going
to morning practice, too.

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:14.720
Something's up with him.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:19.740
I mean, he's a teenager now.
He's probably got a lot going on.

00:24:00.900 --> 00:24:02.500
It's "friends," yeah?

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:04.000
It's "hard work," 'n' "guts"!

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.040
It's "diet" and uh...

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:07.840
"Adoration," I think?

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:09.550
There's no one word for it.

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:12.020
The good times and the bad.

00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:14.200
Because we've got baseball.

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:14.760
Yeah!

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:15.600
That's right!

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:17.050
Because we've got baseball!

00:24:17.050 --> 00:24:17.970
That's why...

00:24:17.970 --> 00:24:18.970
Next time:

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:20.430
"...With You Again!"

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:21.450
All together now:

00:24:21.450 --> 00:24:24.040
Run to the stage of your dreams!

00:24:21.730 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>...With You Again</b>
